1
00:00:32,727 --> 00:00:38,727
Vincent is a animation, fantasy film directed by Tim Burton.

2
00:01:05,454 --> 00:01:11,454
Young Vincent Malloy dreams of being just like Vincent Price and loses
himself in macabre daydreams that annoy his mother.

3
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:44,181
Narrator (voice), played by Vincent Price.

4
00:02:10,909 --> 00:02:16,909
Vincent is a 1982 American gothic stop-motion animated short film written,
designed and directed by Tim Burton, and produced by Rick Heinrichs.

5
00:02:43,636 --> 00:02:49,636
The film is narrated by actor Vincent Price, a
lifelong idol of and inspiration for Burton.

6
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:22,363
From this relationship, Price would go on to appear
in Burton's Edward Scissorhands.

7
00:03:49,090 --> 00:03:55,090
Vincent Price later said that Vincent was "the most
gratifying thing that ever happened.

8
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:27,818
It was immortality — better than a star on Hollywood Boulevard."
There is currently
no individual release of the film except for a few bootleg releases.

9
00:04:54,545 --> 00:05:00,545
It can be found on the 2008 Special Edition and Collector's Edition DVDs of The Nightmare
Before Christmas as a bonus feature and on the Cinema16 DVD American Short Films.

10
00:05:27,272 --> 00:05:33,272
The film explores themes of narration, mama's boy,
stop motion, spoof, black and white.
